   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Did it work?",
   "cap": "DID IT WORK?",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "There's no evidence it did.",
   "cap": "THERE'S *NO EVIDENCE* | IT DID.",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "And historians still argue about how you were even meant to use it.",
   "cap": "AND HISTORIANS | STILL *ARGUE* | ABOUT HOW | YOU WERE EVEN | MEANT TO USE IT.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Good news.",
   "cap": "GOOD NEWS.",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "You no longer need a crocodile.",
   "cap": "YOU *NO* LONGER | NEED A CROCODILE.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Condoms are about ninety eight percent effective,",
   "cap": "CONDOMS ARE ABOUT | *98%* EFFECTIVE,",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "when used correctly.",
   "cap": "WHEN USED *CORRECTLY.*",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "And they also help protect against sexually transmitted infections.",
   "cap": "AND THEY ALSO | HELP *PROTECT* AGAINST | SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED | INFECTIONS.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Crocodile poop does neither.",
   "cap": "CROCODILE POOP | DOES *NEITHER.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "So please.",
   "cap": "SO PLEASE.",
   "pause": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Leave the crocodile alone.",
   "cap": "LEAVE THE | CROCODILE *ALONE.*",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Follow,",
